---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import TokenTable from "../components/api/TokenTable.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "critical", label: "Critical" },
  { id: "actions", label: "Actions and close" },
  { id: "announcing", label: "Announcing changes" },
  { id: "error-summary", label: "Error summary" },
  { id: "tokens", label: "Tokens" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="alert">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          An <code>.alert</code> is a message that stays in the page, next to
          the content it is about, until the problem goes away or the user
          dismisses it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Use a <a href={route("snackbar")}>snackbar</a> for brief feedback
          after an action, and a <a href={route("dialogs")}>dialog</a> when the
          user must decide before going on. An alert holds an optional leading
          icon, then the message: a heading, a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, or both.
        </p>
        <div class="alert mb-3">
          <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">info</span>
          <p>Your trial ends in 3 days. <a href="#tokens">See plans</a></p>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="alert">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">info</span>
  <p>Your trial ends in 3 days. <a href="/plans">See plans</a></p>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.critical}>
        <p>
          <code>critical</code> uses the error container colors for problems
          that stop something from working.
        </p>
        <div class="alert critical mb-3">
          <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">error</span>
          <h4>Payment failed</h4>
          <p>Your card was declined. Update it to keep your workspace active.</p>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="alert critical">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">error</span>
  <h3>Payment failed</h3>
  <p>Your card was declined. Update it to keep your workspace active.</p>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.actions}>
        <p>
          An <code>.alert-actions</code> row puts buttons under the message,
          aligned to the end. An <code>.icon-button</code> as the last child is
          the close button; it stays beside the first line. Closing the alert
          is the page's job: remove it, then move focus to something nearby
          so it does not fall back to the top of the page.
        </p>
        <div class="alert mb-3">
          <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">cloud_off</span>
          <p>You're offline. Edits are saved on this device and sync when the connection returns.</p>
          <div class="alert-actions">
            <button class="button text" type="button">Retry sync</button>
          </div>
          <button class="icon-button" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss">
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
          </button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="alert">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">cloud_off</span>
  <p>You're offline. Edits are saved on this device and sync when the connection returns.</p>
  <div class="alert-actions">
    <button class="button text" type="button">Retry sync</button>
  </div>
  <button class="icon-button" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
  </button>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.announcing}>
        <p>
          An alert that is in the page when it loads needs no role. When one
          appears or changes while the page is in use, put
          <code>role="status"</code> on its text, or <code>role="alert"</code>
          when the user must act now. The live element must already be in the
          page before you write the text into it, and it must not hold the
          buttons: a screen reader would read their labels as part of the
          message. Never use <code>role="banner"</code>, which marks the page
          header.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<div class="alert critical">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">error</span>
  <p role="alert" id="save-error"></p>
  <div class="alert-actions">
    <button class="button text" type="button">Try again</button>
  </div>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["error-summary"]}>
        <p>
          An <code>.error-summary</code> alert at the top of a
          <code>novalidate</code> form lists what is wrong when the form is
          submitted. While any field is invalid the submit stops, as it would
          natively, and the Forms behavior writes one link per invalid field
          into the summary's <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>: the field's label and
          the browser's message. A radio group gets one link, named by its
          legend. Then the summary shows and takes focus, so a screen reader
          reads it. Each link focuses its field. A valid submit hides the
          summary again, and a submit button with
          <code>formnovalidate</code> skips the check.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>novalidate</code> is required. Without it the browser stops an
          invalid form before the submit event, and only the first field's
          bubble appears. Keep each field's own error text too; the summary
          only gathers them.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<form novalidate>
  <div class="alert critical error-summary" hidden aria-labelledby="problem">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">error</span>
    <h2 id="problem">There is a problem</h2>
    <ul></ul>
  </div>
  <label for="email">Email address</label>
  <input id="email" type="email" required>
  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.tokens}>
        <p>Override these on the <code>.alert</code>.</p>
        <TokenTable>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-alert-container-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-secondary-container</code>; critical: <code>--md-sys-color-error-container</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-alert-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-on-secondary-container</code>; critical: <code>--md-sys-color-on-error-container</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-alert-shape</code></td>
            <td>16px</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-alert-padding</code></td>
            <td>16px</td>
          </tr>
        </TokenTable>
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>
